  id: Cervical_part_of_trapezius_muscle.L
  partName: Cervical_part_of_trapezius_muscle.L
  descriptionChunks:
  - This portion of the trapezius muscle supports head and neck movement by stabilizing
    and positioning the cervical region. It assists in lifting, turning, and extending
    the head, allowing for a wide range of motion.
  - ' The muscle also plays a role in maintaining posture by supporting the weight
    of the head. It works in coordination with other neck muscles to ensure smooth
    and controlled movements, especially during activities requiring balance and
    directional changes.'
